# Particles
@scenario tutorial_lesson_23
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide point]
pip: A particle effect draws many small moving sprites. This example uses dust.
[if !tutorial_still]
[particles dust intensity=0.24 opacity=0.52 speed=0.30 duration=3000]
[endif]
pip: Watch the particles against the white background. Reduced motion keeps the example still.
[particles stop]
pip: Change the intensity in the particles command, then replay.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: Which comparison tells you whether the effect helps?
> Read the same line with the effect on and off. -> correct
> Check the particle count alone. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: The reader experiences the composed frame, not a counter. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: The reader experiences the composed frame, not a counter.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_23]
[flag tutorial_done_23]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_3]
